 "spec": "world/crowd-sim.md is canonical prose; this file is the machine contract for the two-layer crowd. Named ambients resolve from ambients.json routines; extras are unnamed non-persistent background pawns (budgets below). v29 adds day shades, the flow layer, micro-texture, continuity rules, the appearance palette, and the greeting matrix. Conditions only — nothing here orders a pawn to do anything. v43 adds the ambient work zones (school/sfgeneral/folsom/auerbach/needlepointe/doloresperk — where the named layer actually spends its days) and ambient_resources — claimable sub-venue slots a request can book without locking the venue. v57 adds the shoulder conditions: the marine layer (fog as a depth profile with a burn-off hour and an all-day mode), afternoon wind, and season shades — the climate baseline the day shades and weather ride on.",
